Thought: First, I'll analyze the molecular formula and spectroscopic data to identify the compound structure. From the elemental analysis, the formula is C23H20O2. The IR shows carbonyl stretches (1693, 1662 cm-1) suggesting ketones. The 1H NMR shows aromatic protons (7.05-7.57, 7.73, 8.03 ppm) and aliphatic signals including a methyl group (1.34 ppm). The 13C NMR shows carbonyl carbons (194.5, 194.8 ppm) confirming two ketone groups. Let me search for compounds with similar spectral properties.
Action: search_by_smiles
Action Input: {"smiles": "CC(C(=O)c1ccccc1)C(=O)c1ccccc1", "top_k": 10}

Thought: Great! The formula C23H20O2 matches the elemental analysis data. Now let me simulate the spectra for this compound to see if it matches the given spectroscopic data.
Action: simulate_spectra
